# {{.project_name}}

Rust Axum API generated by smokeforge.

## Commands

```bash
make install
# commit Cargo.lock after the first install
make run
make test
make check
make build
```

The API serves `/healthz`, `/readyz`, `/api/v1/ping`, `/openapi.json`, and
`/docs`.

## Code layout

```text
src/
  main.rs          process startup, telemetry, listener, graceful shutdown
  lib.rs           router, middleware, OpenAPI composition
  config.rs        typed figment/dotenv configuration
  error.rs         application error type and status mapping
  response.rs      success helpers and RFC 9457 problem responses
  state.rs         cheaply cloneable AppState and readiness seam
  telemetry.rs     tracing subscriber setup
  health/          liveness and readiness routes
  db/              SQLx adapter (database overlay)
  auth/            JWT auth service and routes (auth overlay)
  media/           private S3 media (media overlay)
  search/          Meilisearch adapter (search overlay)
  cache/           Redis adapter (cache overlay)
  queue/           RabbitMQ worker, retries, dedupe (queue/dedupe overlays)
  scheduler/       Redis scheduler leader election (scheduler overlay)
docs/
  API.md           endpoint and error contract
  ARCHITECTURE.md  request flow, module boundaries, extension points
tests/
  api_test.rs      base HTTP integration tests
  response_test.rs response/error integration tests
  auth_db_test.rs  Postgres-backed auth flow (TEST_DATABASE_URL)
  database_test.rs Postgres migration/readiness (TEST_DATABASE_URL)
  common/          shared test helpers
```

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before changing module boundaries, and `CONTEXT.md`
before changing engineering rules. Feature overlays add their own module under
the closest domain and their own documentation.

## Response contract

Use `crate::response` for HTTP response construction:

- `response::ok`, `created`, `accepted`, `json`, and `no_content` for success.
- `AppError` from `crate::error` for failures; `IntoResponse` emits RFC 9457
  problem details.
- `ProblemDetails` includes `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`,
  `code`, `request_id`, and field `errors`.
- `finalize_problem` adds the request path and request ID to errors produced by
  any downstream layer.

Never hand-build an error JSON body in a handler.

See [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) for the project map, runtime diagrams, and change guide.
